n narrative and goal  driven missions the ultimate goal is to  take out El sueño the leader of the  Santa Blanca drug cartel that  essentially runs Bolivia your CIA  contact Karen Bowman also has a  vindictive score to settle as one of her  friends in the DEA was kidnapped and  tortured to death by Santa Blanca while  revenge is a valid enough reason to  upend a narco-state in the clan severs I  suspect that Karen might have other  motives forming squads has been one of  wild lads more intriguing features  during these initial hours in keeping  ghost recons history of team foursomes  having a full squad made up of your  friends is  the ideal experience so far a team of  four humans with at least a modicum of  experience in tactical shooters is a  powerhouse in wild lands even though  enemy head counts adjust to scale with  the size of your team players who  already have a squad in mind might want  to consider starting off the game at the  highest difficulty however playing solo  with a squad of three AI companions  offers its own unique benefits when  coordinating a synchronized skill of  three targets the AI is reasonably  efficient in moving to reach  line-of-sight within seconds and they're  more durable than your friends when  taking fire which is immensely helpful  if they're out into open healing you  what is puzzling is that you can have a  mixed team of humans in AI if you and a  friend are playing a private session you  can't round off your team with two AI  operators what's more amusing is that  you still can hear the story related  banter between all four squad mates  I hate smart drops they make a sloppy  drunk dead there's comfort and falling  into a tactical routine with your  buddies as you reach the perimeter of  every enemy outpost this infiltration  cycle begins when you use your tiny  drone to survey the stronghold and mark  your visible enemies the ability to  track marked enemies through multiple  walls feels like cheating though that  hasn't diminished the appeal of the many  other tom clancy games that use this  feature the openness of wildlands makes  this tactic all the more essential and  helps your team decide on the best  strategy it remains to be seen whether  wildlands retains the same gadget of pl  Ghost Recon Future Soldier later on in  the game though perhaps the drone is all  the advanced tech need in Bolivia in to  ten hours have spent on the road to  liberate Bolivia from El sueño rule of  unlocked 20% of the map as I've slowly  made my way through the hit list of  underlings I've been curious about the  risks of sticking to the critical path  and whether there's such a thing as  being under levelled in wild lands that  said it's been easy to take brief detour  Stern extra experience and kills thanks  to the added efficiency of my teammates  AI controlled or otherwise whatever path  my journey takes I know it will involve  more diversions to earn extra abilities  to take downs of the bosses lieutenants  and the elimination of El sueño himself  which is tomato take an additional 30 to  40 hours stay tuned for our review in  the coming days  Roman this is nomads mantra spoke is  dead  [Music]

